{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytMathlibBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SytMathlibBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytRowSuperstandard","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L204-L212","doc":"**sp09 part 2 — the SYT-count equiv.** `numSYT μ = numStandardYoungTableaux μ`:\nthe bespoke 0-based SYT count equals the Mathlib-SSYT-based count, via the `±1`\nshift bijection `toMathlib`/`toBraidKnot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.toMathlib_toBraidKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.toMathlib_toBraidKnot","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L187-L202","doc":"Right inverse `toMathlib ∘ toBraidKnot = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.mathlibSYT_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.mathlibSYT_ext","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L182-L185","doc":"Mathlib SYT equality reduces to SSYT equality (`bijOn` is a `Prop`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.toBraidKnot_toMathlib","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.toBraidKnot_toMathlib","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L173-L180","doc":"Left inverse `toBraidKnot ∘ toMathlib = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.toMathlib","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau.toMathlib","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L127-L171","doc":"**The one-up conversion** `QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau μ →\nQOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau μ`: shift each on-cell entry up by one (range\n`1..|μ|`), pin off-cell entries to `0`.  Inverse of `toBraidKnot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.col_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.col_mono","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L113-L124","doc":"Arbitrary-gap column strictness from the consecutive `col_strict`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.row_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.row_mono","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L100-L111","doc":"Arbitrary-gap row strictness from the consecutive `row_strict`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instNonemptyBraidKnotStandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instNonemptyBraidKnotStandardYoungTableau","kind":"instance","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**`QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau μ` is nonempty (sorry-free).** Via the\nbridge from the row-superstandard Mathlib SYT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rowSuperstandardBraidKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rowSuperstandardBraidKnot","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L81-L87","doc":"**The row-superstandard tableau as a `QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau`** —\nthe base tableau `T₀` the Okounkov–Vershik exchange argument\n(`syt_all_connect_to_some`) walks every SYT toward, in the exact type that\nargument consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.toBraidKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.toBraidKnot","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SytMathlibBridge.lean#L36-L79","doc":"**The one-down conversion** `QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau μ →\n`QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau μ`: shift each entry down by one so the range\nbecomes `0..|μ|-1`.  Off-diagram entries (`= 0` by `zeros'`) stay `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}